---
const points = [
  'Your broker login credentials are never stored',
  'Your funds statement is read in the browser, and the file itself is never uploaded',
  'Row descriptions are optional, and hashed on arrival when you do send them',
  'Sensitive data is encrypted with Privacy Vault (Databunker)',
  'Only you can access your portfolio data',
  'Trade files are processed and never exposed to third parties',
];
---

<section id="privacy" class="py-24 lg:py-32 bg-navy-800/20">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Data Security</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-cream leading-tight mb-6">
          Your portfolio data<br />
          <em class="font-semibold not-italic">stays yours</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
          We use Privacy Vault, a secure encrypted store, to protect personally identifiable
          information like your name and email. Where a regular database would hold those fields
          in the clear, Privacy Vault locks them with separate encryption keys.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
          The funds statement gets stricter treatment, because its description column carries your
          client code, payment references and bank account. Margin reads that file in your browser
          and sends only the dated amounts, so the file never leaves your machine. Sending the
          description at all is your choice, and when you do, the server hashes it on arrival and
          keeps the hash alone. Nothing reads the wording back, no endpoint returns it, and there is
          no text search over the ledger.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          {points.map((point) => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-muted">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-gold-400 mt-0.5 shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5" />
              </svg>
              {point}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <a
          href="/privacy-vault"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          How Privacy Vault protects you
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5M21 12H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2 flex justify-center">
        <div class="relative w-72 h-72">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 rounded-full border border-border animate-pulse opacity-30"></div>
          <div class="absolute inset-6 rounded-full border border-gold-400/20 animate-pulse opacity-60" style="animation-delay: 0.5s"></div>
          <div class="absolute inset-12 rounded-full border border-gold-400/30"></div>
          <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center">
            <div class="w-28 h-28 rounded-full bg-navy-800 border border-gold-400/30 flex items-center justify-center shadow-lg shadow-gold-400/10">
              <img
                src="/assets/images/privacy-vault.webp"
                alt="Privacy Vault"
                width="256"
                height="256"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
                class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover opacity-80"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
